                  <provenance type="#e"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_2">Peterborough,
                        Northamptonshire. Benedictine abbey of St Peter, St Paul, and St
                        Andrew</orgName><p>The corresponding Medieval Libraries of Great Britain
                        index card records the following evidence:</p><p>At end, erased: <q>Liber
                           fratris Rogerus <note type="editorial">(sic)</note> Birdie monachi</q>.
                        Contemporary inscription: <q>Epistole Pauli <persName role="fmo">Roberti de
                              Nouelle</persName></q>. For <persName role="fmo">Bird</persName>,
                        compare British Library Add MS 39758 and the printed book at Dulwich.
                        Belonged in s. xvi to <persName role="fmo">Geoffrey Parrysche</persName>,
                        vicar of Lilford, Northants (monk of Peterborough in 1539; cf. W T Mellows,
                           <title>Last days of Peterborough monastery</title>, p. xcvi); instituted
                        to Lilford in 1544 and 63 years of age in 1576 (H. I. Longden,
                           <title>Northamptonshire and Rutland Clergy</title> x (1941), 171).
                        Christopher de Hamel identifies <q>Roberti de Nouelle</q> as the Robertus de
                        Nouelle who witnessed Peterborough charters in the time of Abbot Benedict;
                        cf. <title>Northamptonshire Record Society</title> xx
                     169-70.</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="#rejected"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_404">Norwich, Norfolk,
                        Benedictine cathedral priory of Holy Trinity</orgName><p>This attribution
                        was rejected in the second edition of Medieval Libraries of Great Britain
                        (1964), and there were no relevant changes in the Supplement (1987). The
                        corresponding index card records inscriptions that in fact connect the book
                        with Peterborough (details above).</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Given to Peter Mancroft by <persName
                        role="dnr">William</persName> and <persName role="dnr">Alice
                        Gargrave</persName> before 1682; cf. <title>Norfolk Antiquarian
                        Miscellany</title>, ii (1883), 362.</provenance>
               </history>
